<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">How domains are counted</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Each production domain where the plan key is saved uses one domain slot.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Local and staging sites do not use a slot. By default, up to 3 of them can be active on one key at the same time.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Local sites include <code>localhost</code>, private IP addresses and addresses ending in <code>.local</code> or <code>.test</code>. Staging sites include subdomains such as <code>staging.</code>, <code>dev.</code> or <code>test.</code> and common hosting staging domains.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>You can remove a domain in your wopcart.com account to free its slot and use the key on another site.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Removing the plan key from a site's settings also releases that site's slot.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Plan changes</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Upgrades</strong> take effect immediately. The prorated difference is charged at once.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Downgrades</strong> take effect at your next renewal. You keep your current plan until then.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Plan changes are <strong>not refunded or credited</strong>.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Details: <a href="/plan-changes-refunds/">plan changes, domains and refunds</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Immediate delivery</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Your plan key is digital content delivered right after payment. At checkout, you agree to immediate delivery and confirm that you understand this ends the EU right of withdrawal for this purchase.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">If your plan ends</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Your store returns to the free plan: every feature keeps working, and payments are routed through WopCart's Stripe Connect platform with the 2% fee.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->
